; The sessions pin what only a process shows: exit codes, streams, the
; files a run leaves, two processes contending for the lock. Each drives the
; fixture executable in the environment prelude.sh states.
;
; (locks measurement) serializes the scenarios: each one runs real (if tiny)
; measurements, and a dozen concurrent spinning workers would push the load
; average over the environment gate's threshold on any host — the suite would
; flake itself into inconclusive. The timing verdicts, which only a quiet
; host earns, are in quiet/, outside @runtest. A session that hangs (a
; deadline the fixture's hang mode fails to meet, a nested dune build) is
; stopped after 300 s.

(cram
 (locks measurement)
 (timeout 300)
 (deps prelude.sh fixture/bench_fixture.exe fixture/hold_lock.exe))
